<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Munuza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Munuza was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> governor of the Muslim conquerors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gijon">Gijón</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> in the early eighth century. According to the Asturian chronicles, the Visigothic noble Pelagius rebelled against him, and after the Muslim defeat at Covadonga Munuza fled and was caught and killed. The revolt against him marks the beginning of the Kingdom of Asturias.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>According to the Asturian chronicles of the late ninth century, Pelagius, or Pelayo, a Visigothic noble who may have served in the royal guard, was chosen as leader by the Asturians and led a revolt against the Muslim governor <b>Munuza</b> at Gijón.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-asturias">Kingdom of Asturias · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Covadonga, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.31,-5.06&amp;year=764" aria-label="Covadonga on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4428 627 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Munuza"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4878 897h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4878 897h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=43.31,-5.06&amp;year=764">What was here in 764 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
